0,Orokolo language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Orokolo_language,"Orokolo is a Trans–New Guinea language of the Eleman branch spoken in Ihu Rural LLG, Gulf Province, Papua New Guinea by about 50,000 people (2010). Alternate names are Bailala, Haira, Kaipi, Kairu-Kaura, Muro, Muru, Vailala, and West Elema. [1]",Orokolo,Trans-New Guinea
1,"VALS _ Akore _ Orokolo _ Songs - YouTubeOROKOLO_BAY SLAZZII X SKINNY_GEE 2025 PROD BY NB ... - YouTubeOrokolo language - Wikipediapapuan gulf drum orokolo new guinea""KAVAVA - AKAHUS STRINGBAND OF HURURU, OROKORO BAY""""ANOTHER STRINGBAND MUSIC from GULF PROVINCE ... - FacebookLanguage: Orokolo - transnewguinea.org",https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_ATEEUPZuvA,"Feb 18, 2025 · Enjoy the videos and music you love, upload original content, and share it all with friends, family, and the world on YouTube. OROKOLO_BAY SLAZZII X SKINNY_GEE 2025 PROD BY NB RECORDS PNG MUSIC - YouTube Orokolo is a Trans–New Guinea language of the Eleman branch spoken in Ihu Rural LLG, Gulf Province, Papua New Guinea by about 50,000 people (2010). Alternate names are Bailala, Haira, Kaipi, Kairu-Kaura, Muro, Muru, Vailala, and West Elema. [1] Papuan Gulf drum decorated with ancestor faces. The open-mouth carving represents the concept of an instrument ""speaking."" ""Among the Orokolo, the masked hevehe dancers themselves played drums. This is a local stringband music recorded live at Hururu Village in the beautiful Orokolo Bay, Ihu LLG in Gulf Province of Papua New Guinea. The music video was also filmed on location and produced by Niugini Digital Films as it's community incentive whilst on official engagement with TOTAL E&P PNG Ltd, the developer of Papua LNG Project. Dec 25, 2025 · ""ANOTHER STRINGBAND MUSIC from GULF PROVINCE"" Another stringband music coming all the way from featuring Akahus Stringband of Hururu Village alongside the stretchy beautiful black sandy beach ⛱️ of Orokolo Bay in Ihu, Gulf Province. Map: Resources: Glottolog page for Orokolo Ethnologue page for Orokolo Open Language Archives search for Orokolo Wikipedia page for Orokolo Multitree language relationships for Orokolo Glottolog resources for Orokolo",Orokolo,Trans-New Guinea
